  "description": "Alterations and extensions to roof including side and rear dormers; roof light in side roof slope (Retrospective)",
  "epc_number": null,
  "ward": "Belmont",
  "last_updated": "2026-11-18T11:17:00.718Z",
  "street_name": "THE RIDGEWAY",
  "decision_conditions": [
    "&lt;p&gt;&lt;span data-teams=&quot;true&quot;&gt;The alterations and extensions to the roof, by reason of their bulk, visual obtrusiveness and poor design quality, including a lack of separation and subordination of the side and rear elements to the visually prominent front roofslope, the cramped design of the rear dormer, and the lack of separation between the crown roof and rear dormer roof elements, results in a roof structure that&amp;nbsp;&lt;span data-teams=&quot;true&quot;&gt;is representative of poor design and is overly bulky, visually obtrusive and incongruous to the streetscene and is therefore detrimental the character and appearance of the area&lt;/span&gt;, contrary to&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;the high design aspirations of the National Planning Policy Framework (NPPF) 2026, Policy D3 of The London Plan, and Policy GR1 of the Harrow Local Plan (2021-2041).&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;"
